RESULT
  With a USER-DEFINED SSM range (239.100.0.0/16, NOT the default 232.0.0.0/8), a
  group inside that range is handled as Source-Specific Multicast: an IGMPv3
  (S,G) INCLUDE join installs source-specific state and the group is delivered
  from the joined source only.
      IGMPv3 join (S=10.10.81.20, G=239.100.0.10) -> Group mode: Include, Fwd Yes
      source 10.10.81.20 -> G received on receiver ...... 19/20
      mroute is a pure (S,G) with the correct iif/oif  ... yes             => PASS.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BENCH / TOPOLOGY AS TESTED   (PIM-SM/SSM domain, u4 = DUT)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  DUT / PIM-SSM router : u4  S/N 264A23052  MAC 84e3.2787.09c0
      user SSM range   : access-list 40 permit 239.100.0.0 0.0.255.255
                         ip pim ssm range 40
  Host (one NIC, tagged sub-ifs on u4 port1.0.2):
      source   : eth2.81  10.10.81.20  (vlan81)      = the source S
      receiver : eth2.82  10.10.82.20  (vlan82)      = IGMPv3 SSM joiner
  Group under test     : 239.100.0.10   (inside the user range)

METHOD / SCOPE
  No IXIA.  The receiver sends a real scapy IGMPv3 membership report,
  CHANGE_TO_INCLUDE {S} for the group, so the router installs (S,G) INCLUDE state.
  The source transmits to the group; receipt is counted.  SSM semantics are proven
  from the IGMP group detail (Include mode + explicit source list) and the (S,G)-only
  mroute.  Functional test.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG APPLIED   (added to the PIM-SM base; running-config only)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
u4
  access-list 40 permit 239.100.0.0 0.0.255.255
  ip pim ssm range 40
  (base: ip multicast-routing; service pim; interfaces vlan81/vlan82 ip igmp +
   ip pim sparse-mode; IGMP version 3 = platform default.)

